# Exam track — Theme: Akafe Goen (Going Shopping) — Sub-lesson 2: Key Phrases
# Plain sentences (no @question): presented in either direction.
# Mixed with the vocabulary these phrases lean on, so sessions alternate
# word-match and sentence-builder slots.
#
# A1–A2 only: present tense, simple main clauses, no attributive adjectives
# on masculine nouns (avoids declension the learner has not met).

@lesson S1.02 "Shopping Phrases"

@word d'Kaddoen = the presents
@word d'Schong = the shoes
@word d'Tuten = the bags
@word d'Präisser = the prices
@word d'Buttecker = the shops
@word d'Zäit = the time
@word d'Kéier = the time (occasion)
@word alles = everything
@word bëssen = a little
@word soss = otherwise
@word no = near
@word wäit = far

@sentence
@lu Ech brauch eng Tut, wann ech glift.
@en I need a bag, please.
@distractor-lu Kuerf
@distractor-lu kréien
@distractor-en basket
@distractor-en get

@sentence
@lu Wéi vill kascht dat?
@en How much does that cost?
@distractor-lu bezuelen
@distractor-lu wéini
@distractor-en pay
@distractor-en when

@sentence
@lu De Supermarché ass e Sonndeg zou.
@en The supermarket is closed on Sunday.
@distractor-lu Bäckerei
@distractor-lu Samschdeg
@distractor-en bakery
@distractor-en Saturday

@sentence
@lu Ech hunn meng Lëscht doheem vergiess.
@en I forgot my list at home.
@distractor-lu Portmonni
@distractor-lu Tut
@distractor-en wallet
@distractor-en bag

@sentence
@lu D'Uebst um Maart ass bëlleg.
@en The fruit at the market is cheap.
@distractor-lu Geméis
@distractor-lu deier
@distractor-en vegetables
@distractor-en expensive

@sentence
@lu Ech kafen ee Kilo Grompere.
@en I am buying one kilo of potatoes.
@distractor-lu Tomaten
@distractor-lu zwee
@distractor-en tomatoes
@distractor-en two

@sentence
@lu Kann ech mat der Kaart bezuelen?
@en Can I pay by card?
@distractor-lu Geld
@distractor-lu Bong
@distractor-en cash
@distractor-en voucher

@sentence
@lu Dat ass ze deier fir mech.
@en That is too expensive for me.
@distractor-lu bëlleg
@distractor-lu him
@distractor-en cheap
@distractor-en her

@sentence
@lu Ech sichen e Kaddo fir meng Mamm.
@en I am looking for a present for my mother.
@distractor-lu Papp
@distractor-lu kafen
@distractor-en father
@distractor-en buy

@sentence
@lu D'Bäckerei ass net wäit vun hei.
@en The bakery is not far from here.
@distractor-lu Apdikt
@distractor-lu no
@distractor-en pharmacy
@distractor-en near

@sentence
@lu Ech hunn net genuch Geld mat.
@en I do not have enough money with me.
@distractor-lu Zäit
@distractor-lu vill
@distractor-en time
@distractor-en much
